  "key_findings": [
    "Validation split has 0 group_id overlap with training split (dataset-level OOD by text groups).",
    "v6.4.1 recovers v6.3 peak val_proto_acc while reducing train/val overfitting gap.",
    "Need stronger experiment artifact retention to avoid overwritten checkpoints/histories.",
    "Temperature regularization is COUNTERPRODUCTIVE: model needs high temp (~20) for sharp discrimination in 1088-class zero-overlap setting.",
    "Removing cell whitening destroys contrastive learning (raw cell cosine ~0.991).",
    "v7.2 missed temp_lr_multiplier=5.0 (defaulted to 10.0), explaining 1.1pp regression; cohesion 0.25 may also be slightly too aggressive.",
    "Top-10 val_proto_acc (38.2%) is a more stable metric than top-1 (9.3%) for tracking progress.",
    "Explicit group_id propagation from dataset (bypassing cosine detection) improves accuracy: 9.72% vs 8.88% (+0.84pp). Preserves all 1088 groups instead of merging ~40 near-duplicates.",
    "Caption variant augmentation (prob=0.3) is INCOMPATIBLE with prototype-based loss: text_rep for each group becomes noisy (30% chance of variant), degrading alignment targets.",
    "Combined regularization (MixUp + R-Drop + variants + high noise + label smoothing + temp_cap=50) completely kills training — temperature cannot recover.",
    "Mean text_rep (scatter_add average) approach for PrototypeSigLIPLoss is worse than first-cell approach — dilutes gradient signal, temp stuck at 4.2.",
    "The 4x training speedup from explicit group_ids (no O(B²) cosine detection) is a significant engineering win."
  ]
}